WEBVTT

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:28.480
<i>It is a hundred years ago.</i>

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.190
<i>Jean and Nadia escaped from the sinking Nautilus.</i>

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:36.700
<i>Together with Marie and King, they drifted ashore on a desert island.</i>

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:40.740
<i>They had been living comfortably on the Nautilus.</i>

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:44.870
<i>Now they have to live on their own.</i>

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:48.880
<i>Nadia loves the thought of living on a desert island.</i>

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.290
<i>She thinks she can live her whole life there,</i>

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:55.260
<i>because she doesn't know anything about the terrible power of nature.</i>

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:58.220
<i>Just what is she thinking?</i>

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:32.540
What's that?

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:40.550
What is it, Nadia?

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:42.680
Marie's still sleepy.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:46.640
Wake up, everybody! Your eyes will melt if you sleep too much!

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:51.810
We had such a hard time yesterday.

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:55.730
We're going to live on this island from now on.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:58.570
We must change our living schedule.

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:03.530
We must name this island first.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:05.490
I've been considering it.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.450
What is it?

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:09.160
Lincoln Island!

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:11.420
Lincoln Island?

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:15.130
The name of the American president who liberated the black slaves?

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:18.050
That's right. And this inlet is the Captain's Creek!

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:19.590
Captain's Creek?

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:22.010
Because the captain's cabin drifted ashore here?

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:25.430
That's correct! And the beach over there will be Namaki Beach!

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:27.600
Namaki Beach?

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:30.890
After Nadia, Marie and King?

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:31.560
That's right!

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:36.860
Why didn't you include my name?

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:42.610
Namaki is after Nadia, Marie and King, isn't it?

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:45.030
Why not my name?

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.450
Then... NaJaMaKi Beach...

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:50.410
It's hard to say.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:55.290
Oh well! We'll get used to it soon.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:56.040
Right, King?

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:02.470
I think there are more important things to worry about than names.

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:09.020
You don't have to use the names if you don't like them.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:12.980
What's happened to you? You don't seem to be the same Nadia.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:17.480
Jean, I became a new girl after deep consideration last night.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:21.320
I won't worry myself anymore. I won't get angry either.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:24.910
I've cast off my old skin and become a better person.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.330
I'm no longer the Nadia you knew.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:32.250
Yes! I'm Nadia of the Southern Island!

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:37.670
I've outgrown the pupal stage and am now a butterfly!

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:39.880
Good morning, Mr. Shearwater!

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:43.340
Good morning, Mrs. Bunny!

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:48.140
Good morning, animals of the forest!

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:52.730
Nadia, did you bring us here just to say that?

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:54.690
What do you mean?

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:57.310
We have lots of work to do.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:59.520
We have to remove everything from the captain's cabin.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:01.900
We should prepare to survive until help arrives.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:06.610
I have decided to live without science or civilization.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:09.580
So we don't have to do what you've said.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:13.040
From now on, I'm going to live with the forest and nature.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:14.750
Goodbye, Jean!

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:23.130
What's wrong? Nobody's following me.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:25.470
Well, I'm going even if I have to go alone.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:30.930
She's acting funny!

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:37.640
What is this?

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:41.850
This thing? It's a seawater distillation apparatus.

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:44.360
You know we can't drink seawater.

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.610
So we boil it.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:52.110
The salt remains here.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:56.450
The boiled water becomes steam,

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:59.620
condenses back into water, and drips down into this basin.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:01.540
The fresh water is then ready to drink!

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:03.370
Well? Isn't my invention amazing?

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:07.000
Well, how much is ready?

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:25.060
Jean! Jean!

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:26.610
Hurry up! Hurry up!

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.070
Hurry up, won't you?

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:32.700
Jean, we can see a ship!

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:41.200
What's that?

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:57.050
Jean, you don't believe in the power of nature or animals.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:09:00.810
If you stay on this island, you'll regret for the rest of your life

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:03.600
that you believed in science.

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:05.600
This can't be!

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:08.190
Where's Marie? And King?

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:15.780
Goodbye, Jean. We'll live happily with nature.

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:18.530
Wait! Take me with you!

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.080
Wait for me!

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:23.660
Goodbye!

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:25.500
Wait! Wait for me!

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:28.880
Nadia! Wait for me, Nadia!

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:30.880
Don't leave me alone!

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:40.600
It was a dream?

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:43.770
Jean, a ship!

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:45.770
I made this for just such an event!

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:10.840
I made it for an opportunity like this.

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:23.180
What's wrong, King?

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:28.190
Nadia!

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:46.000
Geez...

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.160
She's such a stubborn girl.

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:11.770
Nadia...

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:17.690
Nadia...

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:28.080
Nadia...

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:32.630
Oh, this is very convenient!

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:35.790
I wonder who invented this.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:37.090
It's amazing.

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:40.760
You didn't know about can openers, Jean?

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:42.550
Everyone on the Nautilus knew about it.

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:43.930
Geez!

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:46.890
It's because you don't help your mother.

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:48.020
Right, King?

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:53.940
Anyway, we don't have to ask King to open the cans anymore.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:00.740
Now, let's eat!

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:13.170
How can I

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:17.880
open this thing?

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:23.340
What are these?

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:26.850
These are what the Oriental cultures call chopsticks.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:33.640
They're pretty handy if you're used to them.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:35.770
You'll get skillful with your fingers too.

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:38.480
If you're used to them?

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:42.030
Handy things make your life more comfortable.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:47.660
I don't need gadgets!

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:53.710
I have the guts from my training in the circus to help me win!

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.420
Thanks for the food!

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.180
Nadia's late.

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:16.940
There's nothing to eat out there.

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:18.900
She should come back.

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:20.860
Yeah...

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:26.570
You're like a husband waiting for the wife to come home.

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:30.660
We must find food ourselves from now on.

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:33.870
These were the last ones we brought from the captain's cabin.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:36.330
How about the cans of food I found?

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:39.290
Those are too old. The covers are swollen.

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:41.550
That means it's rotten inside.

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:44.210
Really? Darn it.

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:54.600
Are we going to have fish for lunch?

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:56.100
If we can catch some.

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:59.060
I wish I could eat some meat.

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:04.400
But there's a very scary spirit in the forest.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:10.870
Wait and see!

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:13.410
I'll never give up!

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:45.320
We can't catch a thing.

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:49.610
He did it!

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:51.530
Great, King!

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:52.570
You did it!

00:14:57.700 --> 00:14:59.000
Why did you do that?

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:01.460
It was big!

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:05.340
Big... big... big!

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:06.920
Oh! I got it!

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:09.720
Big fish are in the offing!

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:35.990
How I envy you, Jean.

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:38.250
You have something to play with.

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:41.170
This isn't a toy, Marie.

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:42.670
It's an encyclopedia.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:46.590
This book tells about everything in the world from philosophy to space.

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:49.970
There's also a book of important people, and one of maps too.

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:52.680
Say, Jean, will you make me a toy?

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:53.470
Later, okay?

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:55.220
Oh, I'm so bored!

00:15:57.810 --> 00:15:58.680
Say, King!

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:01.600
Let's play Shiritori!

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:07.520
Okay, I'll begin! Let's see, "Marie", so "ii"!

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:10.990
Ii... Iinyah!

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:14.450
Well, then how about ice cream?

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:17.450
Minyah!

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:19.410
Oh? Almond!

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:20.370
Dinyah!

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:24.210
Iron, oh wait that ends in "n".
So, how about apricot?

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:24.920
Tsunyah!

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:26.340
Asparagus!

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:27.380
Sunya!

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:28.550
Apple pie!

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:29.210
Inya!

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:30.800
Abalone!

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:31.840
Nyah!

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:32.720
Ant!

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:33.220
Tinyah!

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:34.890
Auk!

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:36.390
Amazon!

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:41.430
You don't play fair, King!

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:44.100
Every word you say ends with "nyah"!

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:47.020
You're no fun!

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:49.150
Let's play, Jean! Okay?

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:50.610
Later, okay?

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:54.030
I want to play now!

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:55.070
Later, later.

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:01.410
Got one!

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:07.250
It's a big one!

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:16.090
Wow! It's huge!

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:24.640
HUGE!

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:30.150
A ship!

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:35.030
Third time's the charm!

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:39.530
HEY!

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:41.580
We're over here!

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:45.040
HEY!

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:48.710
HEY! HEY!

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:50.000
Let's stop, Marie.

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:52.000
Why?

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:54.720
Nadia won't leave.

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:14.030
What a pity.

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:16.530
They say it's always the fish you lose that's the biggest.

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:26.290
More destruction of nature.

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:29.420
A ship?

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:46.850
We made a big haul!

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:52.110
Geez, and I had a hard time drying this out.

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:57.030
Help me! Somebody!

00:18:57.360 --> 00:18:59.530
Help me!

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:04.910
It's Nadia! She's being pulled out to sea on the captain's cabin!

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:11.170
It's no use! I'm going to be carried away by the ocean!

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:15.800
Please, animals of the forest, help me!

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:20.970
Please, fish of the sea!

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:29.850
Why? Why doesn't anybody help me?

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:37.440
Jean...

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:42.410
Nadia!

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:53.130
That was very dangerous, Nadia.

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:56.630
That's why no fish came to help me.

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:00.590
You caught all of them!

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:02.380
But...

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:03.550
We couldn't help it!

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:07.810
We'd starve to death if we didn't!

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:09.520
Marie...

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:12.520
The fish understand that!

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:37.750
Why were you in the captain's cabin?

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:42.720
Jean, you brought the hologram with you for me.

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:46.680
It's very important to you, isn't it?

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:49.640
Thank you.

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:54.480
I'm sorry. I was selfish.

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:57.480
I guess I'm awfully stubborn.

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:01.610
We can't live alone with nature.

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:08.030
In order to remain human beings,

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:11.450
we must make things in order to live with nature.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:19.460
Two hundred million years ago, it was the reptilian age on Earth.

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:25.510
They changed the environment to suit their own convenience.

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:28.300
They proliferated enormously and finally destroyed themselves.

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:31.260
Just like human beings now.

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:37.940
So, we must find the science if we're ever to coexist with nature.

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:41.900
Reptilian blood is cold, but human blood is warm.

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:45.990
I want to believe not just in science, but also in human beings.

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:48.370
Jean...

00:21:48.370 --> 00:21:49.120
What?

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:50.370
What's wrong?

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:52.830
Look at this.

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:56.960
Marie has written it.

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:58.580
When did she do this?

00:21:59.840 --> 00:22:02.170
My name is Marie.

00:22:02.170 --> 00:22:08.340
I was born on April 10, 1885, in Marseilles, France.

00:22:08.340 --> 00:22:11.810
But I don't remember anything about Marseilles,

00:22:11.810 --> 00:22:17.270
because we moved to Mahar in the Cape Verde Islands.

00:22:18.020 --> 00:22:20.730
Papa and Mama died there,

00:22:21.110 --> 00:22:25.190
but I'm okay because I'm not alone!

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:29.870
Nadia is my sister.

00:22:29.870 --> 00:22:32.740
She gets angry easily. She has so many likes and dislikes.

00:22:32.740 --> 00:22:37.660
She says she can talk to animals, but I haven't seen it yet.

00:22:37.660 --> 00:22:40.630
But I love her so much!

00:22:41.130 --> 00:22:43.340
Jean is Nadia's husband.

00:22:43.340 --> 00:22:46.090
They are always fighting.

00:22:46.090 --> 00:22:50.760
When I call it a lover's quarrel, they get angry.

00:22:50.760 --> 00:22:52.260
Isn't that mean?

00:22:52.640 --> 00:22:54.760
Jean is always making funny toys,

00:22:54.760 --> 00:22:58.810
but he always says "later" whenever I ask him to play with me.

00:22:59.640 --> 00:23:02.360
He doesn't get angry as easily as Nadia.

00:23:02.360 --> 00:23:04.480
I love him so much!

00:23:04.980 --> 00:23:07.110
King is my husband.

00:23:07.110 --> 00:23:12.320
He was Nadia's boyfriend first, but I stole him away from her.

00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:16.290
He says he loves me more.

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:19.370
We love each other so much.

00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:23.380
Even though he acts a little bit old for his age, I love him so much!

00:23:24.210 --> 00:23:25.880
What is this?

00:23:25.880 --> 00:23:28.210
I have so many likes and dislikes, and get angry easily?

00:23:29.510 --> 00:23:30.430
She's right.

00:23:31.300 --> 00:23:32.140
Jean!

00:23:32.390 --> 00:23:34.100
See? You just got angry!

00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:37.060
I'm not angry yet!

00:23:37.600 --> 00:23:40.980
I know I am mischievous, precocious,

00:23:40.980 --> 00:23:43.150
careless and sentimental.

00:23:43.150 --> 00:23:48.740
But everybody loved me when I was in the circus!

00:23:48.740 --> 00:23:50.950
Geez, don't be so snooty.
